  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'schemabench_0164' contains 9 tables. The 'Customer' table is used to store customer information, including their ID, home store, first name, email, since when they joined, their loyalty card number, birthdate, gender, and birth year. The 'Generation' table contains information about the birth year and generation of customers.\nThe 'Product' table holds information about various products, including their ID, group, category, type, name, description, unit of measure, wholesale price, retail price, tax exempt status, promo status, and new product status. The 'Date' table contains information about various dates, including the transaction date, date ID, week ID, week description, month ID, month name, quarter ID, quarter name, and year ID.\nThe 'Pastry_Inventory' table records the inventory of pastries sold at various sales outlets, including the sales outlet ID, transaction date, product ID, start of day, quantity sold, waste, and waste percentage. The 'Sales_Target' table sets sales targets for various sales outlets, including the sales outlet ID, year and month, beans goal, beverage goal, food goal, merchandise goal, and total goal.\nThe 'Sales_Outlet' table contains information about various sales outlets, including their ID, type, size, address, city, state, telephone number, postal code, longitude, latitude, manager, and neighborhood. The 'Staff' table holds information about the staff, including their ID, first name, last name, position, start date, and location.\nFinally, the 'Sales_Receipt' table records sales receipts, including the transaction ID, date, time, sales outlet ID, staff ID, customer ID, whether the transaction was in-store or not, order number, line item ID, product ID, quantity, line item amount, unit price, and whether the item was a promo item or not.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe coffee industry has experienced significant changes due to the COVID-19 pandemic, with reduced in-store visitors but increased demand for coffee delivery and takeaway to support people working from home. This situation necessitates a robust approach to managing operational data, specifically through implementing a data warehouse to optimize operations during various business hours.\n\n Objectives\n\n- Design a data warehouse dimensional model for analyzing operating hours in the coffee industry.\n- Enhance decision-making regarding sales, inventory, and customer engagement.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Coffee Shop Owners/Managers: Requires insights into operations, sales, and inventory.\n- Data Analysts: Utilize the data warehouse to extract meaningful insights.\n- Operational Staff: Manage sales outlets and customer engagement efficiently.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Customer Management: Maintain comprehensive customer profiles including loyalty and preferences.\n2. Product Tracking: Categorize and manage products with detailed information on pricing, promotions, and descriptions.\n3. Sales and Inventory Analysis: Track daily sales, inventory changes, waste management, and targets across outlets.\n4. Sales Outlet Management: Capture detailed outlet information including location, size, and management details.\n5. Staff Management: Maintain staff information related to roles, locations, and start dates.\n6. Transaction Handling: Record sales receipts and transaction details across outlets, capturing in-store and online sales.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Support expansion to accommodate more outlets and increased data volume.\n- Security: Protect sensitive customer and financial data.\n- Data Accuracy: Ensure high data integrity and minimal errors in reporting.\n- Performance: Enable fast data retrieval and report generation even under heavy load.\n- Reliability: Maintain consistent data updates and system uptime to support seamless operations.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_deepseek/0164.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0164\nCREATE TABLE `Customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `home_store_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `joined_since` date NOT NULL,\n  `loyalty_card_number` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birthdate` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birth_year` int(4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Generation` (\n  `generation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `birth_year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  `generation_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`generation_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `product_group` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_of_measure` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `wholesale_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `retail_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `tax_exempt` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `promo_status` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `new_product_status` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Date` (\n  `date_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `transaction_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `week_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `week_description` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `month_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `month_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `quarter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quarter_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `year_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`date_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Pastry_Inventory` (\n  `sales_outlet_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `transaction_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_of_day` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity_sold` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `waste` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `waste_percentage` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sales_outlet_id`, `transaction_date`, `product_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pastry_inventory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `Product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Sales_Target` (\n  `sales_outlet_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `year` int(4) NOT NULL,\n  `month` int(2) NOT NULL,\n  `beans_goal` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `beverage_goal` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `food_goal` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `merchandise_goal` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `total_goal` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sales_outlet_id`, `year`, `month`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Sales_Outlet` (\n  `sales_outlet_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `outlet_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `size` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `telephone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `postal_code` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(10,8) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(10,8) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `manager` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `neighborhood` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`sales_outlet_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Staff` (\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`staff_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Sales_Receipt` (\n  `transaction_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `date` date NOT NULL,\n  `time` time NOT NULL,\n  `sales_outlet_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `in_store` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,\n  `order_number` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `line_item_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `line_item_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `promo_item` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`transaction_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_receipt_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sales_outlet_id`) REFERENCES `Sales_Outlet` (`sales_outlet_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_receipt_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `Staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_receipt_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `Customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `sales_receipt_ibfk_4` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `Product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
